libpcap (nmap's copy): the package's name and version back in configure

nmap's copy of libpcap renames VERSION to VERSION.txt, and its generated
configure lost the name and version with it (AC_INIT reads VERSION.txt with
m4_esyscmd_s when autoconf runs, and nmap's build never asks for them). Without
them pcap_lib_version() says "libpcap version  (...)", and libpcap.pc has an
empty Version and "-l" for "-lpcap". These are what AC_INIT(pcap, 1.10.7) sets.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index a6d6224..a238445 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -606,10 +606,10 @@ MFLAGS=
 MAKEFLAGS=
 
 # Identity of this package.
-PACKAGE_NAME=''
-PACKAGE_TARNAME=''
-PACKAGE_VERSION=''
-PACKAGE_STRING=''
+PACKAGE_NAME='pcap'
+PACKAGE_TARNAME='pcap'
+PACKAGE_VERSION='1.10.7'
+PACKAGE_STRING='pcap 1.10.7'
 PACKAGE_BUGREPORT=''
 PACKAGE_URL=''
 
